  data: {
    LLM: 'Fold if you see many high cards (Aces, Kings, Queens) on other players. Call or raise if you see mostly low cards. Remember that you cannot see your own card.\n\nConsider the number of players - with more players, the chance someone has a high card increases. Use position to your advantage - acting last gives more information. Watch betting patterns for tells.\n\nGame theory optimal play involves randomizing between calling and folding in marginal situations. Against skilled opponents, use mixed strategies. Consider pot odds relative to the probability your card is highest based on visible cards.',
    Player: 'Fold if you see many high cards (Aces, Kings, Queens) on other players. Call or raise if you see mostly low cards. Remember that you cannot see your own card.\n\nConsider the number of players - with more players, the chance someone has a high card increases. Use position to your advantage - acting last gives more information. Watch betting patterns for tells.\n\nGame theory optimal play involves randomizing between calling and folding in marginal situations. Against skilled opponents, use mixed strategies. Consider pot odds relative to the probability your card is highest based on visible cards.',
